---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Terms of Service Page
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | December"
  description="Terms of Service for December software, CLI, and cloud execution."
  canonicalUrl="https://trydecember.com/terms"
  activePath="/terms"
  hideHeader={false}
  hideFooter={false}
>
  <!-- Main Container: Identical horizontal gap/margins to landing page and docs page -->
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[940px] px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-24 min-w-0">
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="flex items-center flex-wrap font-mono text-xs text-[#64748b] mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#090a0f] transition-colors">home</a>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">legal</span>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#090a0f] font-medium">[terms]</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Article Layout: Spans full width matching landing page & docs structure -->
    <article class="w-full min-w-0">
      <!-- Document Header -->
      <header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl min-w-0">
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-[#090a0f] leading-snug">
          Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#52525b] leading-relaxed">
          These Terms govern your use of the December CLI, web applications, and cloud workspaces. We believe in clear, fair rules without unnecessary legal jargon.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Markdown / Body Content -->
      <div class="docs-prose min-w-0 max-w-full text-[#52525b] text-sm sm:text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2>Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>
            By downloading, installing, or using December, you agree to these Terms. If you are using December on behalf of an organization or team, you confirm you have permission to agree to these terms for your team.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>License & Usage</h2>
          <p>
            You have the right to install and use December to write, build, test, and ship your software projects. Open-source components are subject to their respective open-source licenses.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your Code Belongs to You</h2>
          <p>
            You own 100% of your source code, repositories, prompts, and all generated outputs:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>December claims zero ownership over anything you build or write.</li>
            <li>All code generated by the agent during your sessions is assigned to you.</li>
            <li>We never use your private code or prompts to train AI models.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Subscriptions & Bring Your Own Key (BYOK)</h2>
          <p>
            When you use your own API keys (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek), you pay your AI provider directly at standard token rates with zero markup from December. Cloud sandbox features are billed according to your subscription plan. You can cancel your subscription at any time.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Cloud Sandboxes & Web Previews</h2>
          <p>
            Cloud workspaces run inside private Linux containers with automatic web previews. You are responsible for any public preview URLs you create and for keeping secrets or API keys out of public links.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to use December or its cloud sandboxes to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Create or distribute malware, viruses, or security exploits.</li>
            <li>Perform unauthorized attacks or denial-of-service against systems.</li>
            <li>Mine cryptocurrency or bypass cloud resource limits.</li>
            <li>Violate applicable laws, privacy rules, or third-party rights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Verify AI Outputs</h2>
          <p>
            December is an AI pair-programming assistant. Like any AI tool, it can occasionally make mistakes or generate imperfect code. You are responsible for testing and reviewing all code changes before deploying them to production. December is provided as-is without warranties of any kind.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Governing Law & Contact</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware. If you have any questions about these terms or custom agreements, email us at
            <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com">team@trydecember.com</a><!--/email_off-->.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Navigation & Contact -->
      <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">
          Questions? <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com" class="text-[#87b2f4] hover:underline">team@trydecember.com</a><!--/email_off-->
        </span>
        <a
          href="/privacy"
          class="group inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 p-2.5 border border-[#e2e8f0] bg-white hover:border-[#87b2f4] text-[#090a0f] transition-all"
        >
          <span>Privacy Policy</span>
          <span class="text-[#94a3b8] group-hover:text-[#87b2f4] transition-colors">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
